academy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is shown below. Notice that the function contains a jump exactly at $x=-2$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/05ad378968e143e83dab8d50608e6db7ccaf97f5e1a8f2ee83d2f893e3d820c3.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs can be plotted without taking the pencil off of the paper." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f0fe659e26fd8a6898c8e4a384044d988b015cc1e9d1eb222fceb862d48a0fc"} {"question" "q-104036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/21e0c66adc999bb5c3837b1d3754695bc77cd00ba48b951f5020a7a43517cac4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/3e494ced6afa7e2c2601ef76c21da08480227d9cbc6305838c004edcc56e431c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/69ad36f502222c0dbed981658b601816ddf40449021a06cb84d03eba82ccf864.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/88b379da88c9c00be0aa64557dfdccef6bd503a894d56f5a89a13b081db2ab14.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/caa67175ab6237629bfb168e98f4399103e03ce603004aed8f23d2d14b01d7a8.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/caa67175ab6237629bfb168e98f4399103e03ce603004aed8f23d2d14b01d7a8.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/bdcfa35fb04028cbff32992b41214c878443d3815b676a0cf046f5a99bd771bd.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=-2$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=f(-2)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-2$ and $f(-2)=5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{-}}f(x) & =5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=5=f(-2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f0fe659e26fd8a6898c8e4a384044d988b015cc1e9d1eb222fceb862d48a0fc"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"} {"question" "q-104124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5cfd4502c036ab527ad66086b792c0611ac2b932f6a2b41f6890842147e205f"}] "usage" {"